6142773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying Fractions by Whole Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1033 2360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050599 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "576878c2-12a4-51b4-9889-1011d89192c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1031 "Dividing Decimals Using the Standard Algorithm" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1033 549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050934 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "72a4f3fd-74ae-5991-918c-b3f68b458c76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092028 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092028 #edb/ref 1071 "The average temperature in Helsinki, Finland, in January $2017$ was $-5.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$. If the average temperature (measured in degrees Celsius) in Yakutsk, Russia, in the same month was eight times lower, what was the average temperature in Yakutsk in January $2017$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092028 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c43effb-b65a-503b-b56a-aac7d499ba0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092028 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the temperature in Yakutsk, we multiply the temperature in Helsinki by $8$. This gives\n\n$$\n(-5.5^{\\circ}\\, \\textrm{C}) \\times 8 = -44^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Yakutsk in January $2017$ was $-44^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092032 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092032 #edb/ref 1071 "Martin has an overdraft facility authorized by his bank. His bank balance at the beginning of the month was $-\\[math] 550$.\n\nTo reduce his debt with the bank, Martin deposited some money into his account. After making the deposit, his new balance was $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ of the initial balance. Then, at the end of the month, Martin made a withdrawal of $\\[/math] 40$.\n\nWhat was Martin's bank balance at the end of the month?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092032 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2111bc1e-b9e1-58b1-873f-d8f94b8446ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092032 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine Martin's bank balance after he made the deposit, we multiply the initial balance by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n(-\\[math] 550) \\cdot \\dfrac{2}{5} =-\\[/math] 220\n$$\n\nMartin's bank balance was updated again when he made a withdrawal. To determine the final balance, we subtract the amount of money he withdrew from $-\\[math]220$. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\[/math] 220 - \\[math] 40 =-\\[/math] 260\n$$\n\nTherefore, Martin's bank balance at the end of the month was $-\\[math] 260$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092150 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092150 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature in a chamber that holds chlorine is $-24\\dfrac{1}{3}{^\\circ}\\textrm{F}$. It's known that chlorine boils at $\\dfrac{6}{5}$ the chamber's temperature measured in degrees Fahrenheit. What is the boiling temperature of chlorine?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092150 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed21898f-dfc1-543a-bf57-313c6e94dd63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092150 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out the boiling temperature of chlorine, we need to calculate\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nas an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-24\\dfrac{1}{3} = -\\dfrac{24\\times 3 + 1}{3} = -\\dfrac{73}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-\\frac{73}{3}) \\cdot \\frac{6}{5} &= -\\frac{73 \\cdot 6}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{73 \\cdot 2}{\\cdot 5} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{146}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{146}{5} = -29\\dfrac15\n$$\n\nTherefore, chlorine boils at\n\n$$\n-29\\dfrac15{^\\circ}\\textrm{F}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying and Dividing Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186092028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092188 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bc5fba78-066d-56fb-b5ac-6733fa0349bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1039 "Combining Operations on Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186092032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092192 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "623e299c-b14a-5fba-aa7e-3fe556be7c6e" 