417] [17592186502066 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5b6c3c0b-b541-5b1f-810b-d9c4ffa1fe9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502067 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502067 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502067 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502067 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186502160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502067 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6d7b67c1-aa22-5106-9f09-19e361dc25c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502068 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502068 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502068 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502068 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186502105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502068 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aec0cd94-20e4-5748-b9c1-4de7b1854a8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502069 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502069 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186502119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502069 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Problems Involving Multiplying Negative Fractions and Mixed Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502069 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186502120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502069 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f589fffd-f5c4-590e-9ed1-01c20390700f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature inside a freezer decreases by $\\frac{3}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $1\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "361640a2-f197-5749-a9e6-5d3176000185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502092 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{3}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $1\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 4+1}{4}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\\times (-\\frac{3}{5})=-\\frac{5\\times 3}{4\\times 5}=-\\frac{15}{20}=-\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502105 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502105 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature of a liquid decreases by $\\dfrac{4}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}$ each minute for $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502105 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f3cfae7-b7d6-56b2-a245-6ec44b76e462" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502105 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $\\dfrac{4}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\dfrac{4}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{2} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{2} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)\n= -\\dfrac{3 \\times 4}{2 \\times 5}\n= -\\dfrac{12}{10}\n= -\\dfrac{6}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-\\dfrac{6}{5}\\,^\\circ\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature in a city decreases by $1.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour for $5$ hours. What is the total change in temperature after $5$ hours?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62ed462d-094a-533c-8c38-e7a5c2d0177d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502107 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $1.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $5$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $1.2:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $5$ hours is $-6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature of a chemical solution decreases by $\\frac{4}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b837a54-b40c-5dbd-9c93-92d2c8b04271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502119 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{4}{5}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{4}{5}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 4+3}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5})=-\\frac{15\\times 4}{4\\times 5}=-\\frac{60}{20}=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-3{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502120 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502120 #edb/ref 1071 "A submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute from sea level. What is the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502120 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7be163d0-2103-5467-9bba-a4090855cc8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502120 #edb/ref 1074 "The submarine descends $1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\,\\text{m}$ each minute.\n\nSince the elevation decreases, the change each minute is $-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}.$\n\nThe descent lasts $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes, so the total change in elevation is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-1\\,\\dfrac{3}{8} = -\\dfrac{1\\times8 + 3}{8} = -\\dfrac{11}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the product:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{8}{3} \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{11}{8}\\right)\n= -\\dfrac{8 \\times 11}{3 \\times 8}\n= -\\dfrac{11}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the submarine's elevation after $\\dfrac{8}{3}$ minutes is $-\\dfrac{11}{3}\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502129 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502129 #edb/ref 1071 "Over the course of $6$ hours, the temperature of a liquid decreases by $9.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ in total. Assuming the temperature decreases at a constant rate, what is the change in temperature each hour?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c400da4-eba5-58aa-8ee5-a33269adfa2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502129 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the temperature decreases by $9.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ over $6$ hours, the total change is $-9.6^\\circ\\text{C}.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $6$ hours, so we divide the total change by $6{:}$\n\n$$\n-9.6 \\div 6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-9.6 \\div 6 = -1.6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature changes by $-1.6^\\circ\\text{C}$ each hour." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357178" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature inside a freezer drops by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ every hour for $4$ hours. What is the total change in temperature after $4$ hours?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b43654ae-4e3f-5d53-a4fb-91c5e392ca63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502136 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $2.5{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $4$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $2.5:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,2.5-2.5-2.5-2.5}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n4\\times (-2.5)=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $4$ hours is $-10{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357219" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1071 "Over $6$ days, $$14.70$ is deducted from a transit card balance due to daily fares of equal size. What is the change in the balance each day?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf763c67-fa75-5f72-8661-230a30b13c07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502147 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the balance decreases by $$14.70$ over $6$ days, the total change is $-$14.70.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $6$ days, so we divide the total change by $6:$\n\n$$\n-14.70÷6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-14.70÷6=-2.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in the balance each day is $-$2.45.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature of a liquid decreases by $\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute for $\\frac{8}{3}$ minutes. What is the total change in temperature?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d71152b6-16b1-5e4e-a992-55dfd11f6205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502152 #edb/ref 1074 "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{3}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $\\frac{8}{3}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{4}).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{8\\times 3}{3\\times 4}=-\\frac{8}{4}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1071 "A diver descends a total of $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes at a constant rate. What is the change in elevation each minute?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e034c9b1-b463-56a2-afff-761ad637fb35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502155 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the diver's elevation decreases by $32.5\\,\\text{m}$ over $5$ minutes, the total change is $-32.5\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nThis change occurs evenly over $5$ minutes, so we divide the total change by $5:$\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-32.5÷5=-6.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change in elevation each minute is $-6.5\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357194" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1071 "A hot air balloon descends $\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ each second. What is the total change in altitude after $\\frac{9}{7}$ seconds?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8734cff-4115-50f2-9d56-00580f475192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502156 #edb/ref 1074 "The hot air balloon descends $\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ each second.\n\nSince the altitude decreases, the change each second is $-\\frac{7}{3}.$\n\nThe descent lasts $\\frac{9}{7}$ seconds, so the total change in altitude is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}\\times (-\\frac{7}{3}).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}\\times (-\\frac{7}{3})=-\\frac{9\\times 7}{7\\times 3}=-\\frac{9}{3}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in altitude is $-3\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502160 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502160 #edb/ref 1071 "A customer opens a bank account with a balance of ![](images/b6/b6d32477e84b569c63644d22eac5c4ac7628d3513fa649efe3b53af4dd46bd63.svg). The account allows overdrafts, and the customer withdraws ![](images/3f/3fb4b29875dcbc25b7a9836d939831543811af3f8b7959c34bbe2ef7c5739187.svg) each day for ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) days. What is the account balance after ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) days?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502160 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f100ae8f-6865-5741-a125-4d55e90e2e43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502160 #edb/ref 1074 "The bank balance decreases by ![](images/3f/3fb4b29875dcbc25b7a9836d939831543811af3f8b7959c34bbe2ef7c5739187.svg) each day.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) days, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of ![](images/34/3474a36d6b0c9f191464fa9f990df13762af9a0c6b5e8138242a195cc33120e6.svg)\n\n![](images/f5/f5fbbe1aa003f39beaa1c8bbc83d1ba09f5588bb3e2a061287093e214f2ffb78.svg)\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n![](images/4d/4db89374d470b00b0463b35e087efbb5ebfd8cbc0e0a408a9bfaf052cd9c5a32.svg)\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n![](images/0a/0a1462b31c3a16cb37e282f254ad252b061aff0534e9bdf5972144d7de7e5a8a.svg)\n\nTherefore, the account balance after ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) days is ![](images/27/27f2d0115060366cb914179f4e2e6e9b0f9ddb29a6530984a105d7a0f5f29f71.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502176 #edb/ref 1061 621937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502176 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a846be7-1beb-5415-afda-c7dbc9dfc761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502176 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502186 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186502187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502186 #edb/ref 1061 621932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502186 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "71ab7d7f-9cc1-5cdf-9b66-2a332d38a8be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502186 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502187 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186502188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502187 #edb/ref 1061 621933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502187 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75f9f2c1-6398-5c11-a04e-b2c1ba8f749f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502187 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502188 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186502210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502188 #edb/ref 1061 621941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502188 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7899018c-d6d5-5a73-8bba-a499b1170d83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502188 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502209 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186502176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502209 #edb/ref 1061 621978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502209 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f88bb973-cdd9-5dc3-a6f0-ee3f3807638e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502209 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502210 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186502209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502210 #edb/ref 1061 621944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502210 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f8abbf23-8275-57f4-b19a-767b1595b9d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502210 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186502069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502215 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes we know the total change in a quantity and want to find how much the quantity changes during each equal time period.\n\nIn these situations, we use division.\n\nFor example, suppose a total of $\\[math]24$ is withdrawn from a bank account over $6$ days in equal amounts.\n\nSince money is withdrawn, the total change in the balance is $-\\[/math]24$.\n\nTo find the change each day, we divide the total change by the number of days:\n\n$$\n-24 \\div 6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-24 \\div 6 = -4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance changes by $-\\[math]4$ each day." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502215 #edb/ref 1065 15182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502215 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2472ba13-0b69-56f2-a477-ea1b2a6fc7e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502215 #edb/ref 1067 "Solving Problems Using Division of Rational Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502216 #edb/ref 1064 "Some real-world situations involve a quantity changing by the same amount repeatedly.\n\nWhen the same change occurs repeatedly, we can represent the total change using multiplication.\n\nFor example, suppose a submarine begins at sea level and descends $2\\,\\text{m}$ each minute for $4$ minutes.\n\nSince descending represents a decrease in elevation, the change each minute is $-2\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nThe total change can be written as repeated subtraction:\n\n![](images/bd/bd6e5218d475c46dd7f0ac578340124954d00fa940c81e32bffa49638b0e79c3.svg)\n\nThis repeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}4} \\times (-2)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n4 \\times (-2) = -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $4$ minutes, the submarine's elevation is $-8\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502216 #edb/ref 1065 15164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502216 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e61ac714-2900-508a-9e66-9731f70e9997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502216 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
